    "city": "nouakchott",
    "climate": "desert",
    "vernacular": "Atlantic-coast Saharan capital built since 1958 on sand: mostly one-storey flat-roofed cement-block houses and compounds rendered in sand, ochre, cream or pastel blue, behind high plastered walls, with wind-blown sand banked against them; broad avenues with sparse trees; 1970s-80s Chinese- and Arab-funded institutional blocks; mosques in white or cream with square or tapering minarets and Moorish arches; recent glass-and-concrete malls and offices in Tevragh Zeina; informal tents (khaima) and shanty districts of cement blocks.",
