    "ornament": "Moorish horseshoe and pointed arches on mosques and villa windows, geometric lattice screens and grilles, painted or relief bands around doors and parapets, square minarets with a simple crown, white/cream rendering against desert sand.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nouakchott",
        "what": "Nouakchott: most buildings are one storey; Kebbe shanty-town buildings are cement made to look permanent; Saudi Mosque and Ibn Abbas mosque noted for architecture and size; fish market on a beach devoted to fishing boats; 2016 airport"
      },
      {
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Museum_of_Mauritania",
        "what": "National museum is a two-storey building built in 1972 by the Chinese, an example of 1970s foreign-aid institutional architecture"
      }
    ]
